  "prefLabel": "He-W 589.03 Student Eligibility",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 589.03 Student Eligibility. To be eligible for medicaid reimbursement for covered services, a student shall:\n\n(a) Have a care plan;\n\n(b) Be between the ages of 3 and 22, provided that the students aged 21 through 22 are not eligible for medicaid reimbursement for services covered only under the EPSDT benefit;\n\n(c) Be a medicaid recipient; and\n\n(d) Be served by an LEA or SAU that is an enrolled school provider.\n\nSource. #4925, INTERIM, eff 8-31-90; ss by #5038, eff 12-28-90; ss by #5456, eff 9-1-92, EXPIRED: 9-1-98\n\nNew. #6861, INTERIM, eff 10-2-98, EXPIRED: 1-30-99\n\nNew. #6987, eff 4-27-99; ss by #8874, INTERIM, eff 4-25-07, EXPIRED 10-22-07\n\nNew. #9035, eff 11-22-07; ss by #11025, eff 1-23-16; ss by #12607, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 8-20-19, EXPIRED: 2-16-19 (and #11025 effective again pursuant to RSA 541-A:18, V); ss by #12861, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 8-28-19\n\nNew. #12994, eff 2-21-20 (formerly He-M 1301.03) (See Revision Note at part heading for He-W 589); ss by #14432, eff 11-25-25, EXPIRES: 11-25-35",
